      "biography": "The Womack Sisters are a Los Angeles-based retro soul and R&B vocal trio made up of sisters BG, Zeimani, and Kucha Womack. They come from one of American music’s most storied families: they are the granddaughters of Sam Cooke, the daughters of Cecil and Linda Womack of Womack & Womack, and the nieces of Bobby Womack.\n\nRaised around music while living in places including London, Amsterdam, Thailand, Kenya, and the Bahamas, the sisters sang from a young age and performed as background vocalists for their parents and uncle before stepping out on their own. They introduced themselves as a trio with self-released singles such as “Darling” and later built momentum with releases including the 2022 EP Legacy, which blended contemporary R&B with a classic soul feel.\n\nTheir sound is rooted in rich harmonies, gospel-inflected emotion, and a throwback aesthetic that recalls girl-group and early soul traditions while still feeling current. After signing with Daptone Records, they continued that approach with music designed to honor their family legacy while establishing their own voice in modern retro soul.",
      "discogs_id": "6484486",
