    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Womack Sisters is the self-titled debut album from The Womack Sisters, released by Daptone in 2026. The trio—Kucha, Zeimani, and BG Womack—draws on a deep soul lineage, and the album presents them as a modern vocal group rooted in classic Funk/Soul tradition, with rich harmonies and lead vocals that each get room to stand out.\n\nThe record pairs a retro-minded sound with a contemporary sense of identity, reflecting the sisters’ upbringing around music and performance while aiming for the emotional weight and melodic clarity associated with vintage soul records. Daptone’s own description emphasizes that the album is the culmination of their long journey, built around “intensely soulful” songs that recall a time when pop music had “substance, vibe and purpose.” The tracklist includes “Chauffeur,” “If You Want Me,” “If I Let You,” “I Just Don’t Want You (To Say Goodbye),” and “You Went Away Too Long,” reinforcing the album’s focus on heartache, resilience, and harmony-driven soul.",
